WEBVTT

00:00:00.302 --> 00:00:02.258
Last video ended with this question.

00:00:02.883 --> 00:00:04.771
Until now, we've known the mean and the

00:00:04.812 --> 00:00:07.122
standard deviation, and found a probability.

00:00:07.847 --> 00:00:09.905
This time the probability is fixed.

00:00:10.591 --> 00:00:12.502
The filling machine has a dial that sets

00:00:12.564 --> 00:00:13.267
the mean fill.

00:00:14.012 --> 00:00:15.953
Only one percent of bottles can be under

00:00:16.054 --> 00:00:18.796
four ninety, sigma stays at eight, and the

00:00:18.857 --> 00:00:20.137
mean is the unknown.

00:00:21.105 --> 00:00:22.316
Where must the dial be set?

00:00:22.963 --> 00:00:24.098
Here's the key idea.

00:00:24.762 --> 00:00:26.905
Turn the dial up, and the bell slides

00:00:26.966 --> 00:00:29.350
to the right, so four ninety ends up

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.413
further out in the tail, and the tail

00:00:31.453 --> 00:00:32.115
gets smaller.

00:00:33.037 --> 00:00:35.181
At a mean of five hundred, the tail

00:00:35.221 --> 00:00:37.466
was zero point one zero five six.

00:00:38.228 --> 00:00:40.315
Fill two hundred bottles there, and in one

00:00:40.397 --> 00:00:42.746
simulated run, nineteen come up short.

00:00:43.551 --> 00:00:45.621
Keep turning, and at some point the tail

00:00:45.723 --> 00:00:47.089
is exactly one percent.

00:00:47.774 --> 00:00:50.550
In sigmas, every normal curve is the same

00:00:50.611 --> 00:00:50.912
curve.

00:00:51.275 --> 00:00:53.683
So a one percent tail always ends the

00:00:53.744 --> 00:00:56.253
same number of sigmas below the mean, whatever

00:00:56.274 --> 00:00:56.775
the mean is.

00:00:57.458 --> 00:00:59.114
That number is a zed score.

00:00:59.679 --> 00:01:01.128
So the job is to find the zed

00:01:01.209 --> 00:01:02.557
first, then the mean.

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:05.435
The table gives areas to the left, for

00:01:05.475 --> 00:01:06.119
positive zeds.

00:01:06.863 --> 00:01:09.153
A one percent tail on the left mirrors

00:01:09.254 --> 00:01:10.780
a one percent tail on the right.

00:01:11.545 --> 00:01:13.716
And a right tail of one percent means

00:01:13.938 --> 00:01:15.546
ninety-nine percent to the left.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:18.802
So search inside the table for zero point

00:01:18.862 --> 00:01:19.425
nine nine.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:22.833
At two point three two it's zero point

00:01:22.914 --> 00:01:23.995
nine eight nine eight,

00:01:24.537 --> 00:01:26.840
and at two point three three it's zero

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:28.603
point nine nine zero one.

00:01:29.386 --> 00:01:31.694
Zero point nine nine zero one is closer,

00:01:32.097 --> 00:01:34.425
so zed is about two point three three.

00:01:35.389 --> 00:01:37.634
Four ninety is below the mean, so zed

00:01:37.675 --> 00:01:39.799
is negative: minus two point three three.

00:01:40.221 --> 00:01:42.110
Now put it into the zed score formula.

00:01:42.632 --> 00:01:45.517
Zed is x minus mu, over sigma, so

00:01:45.817 --> 00:01:48.823
minus two point three three equals four ninety

00:01:48.883 --> 00:01:50.245
minus mu, all over eight.

00:01:50.867 --> 00:01:53.794
Multiply by eight: four ninety minus mu is

00:01:53.974 --> 00:01:55.778
minus eighteen point six four.

00:01:56.361 --> 00:01:58.432
So mu is five hundred and eight point

00:01:58.492 --> 00:01:59.478
six four millilitres.

00:02:00.343 --> 00:02:02.452
With the table's rounding, that leaves a tail

00:02:02.593 --> 00:02:04.782
just under one percent, so it meets the

00:02:04.823 --> 00:02:05.043
limit.

00:02:05.807 --> 00:02:08.110
In words, four ninety has to sit two

00:02:08.191 --> 00:02:11.456
point three three standard deviations, eighteen point six

00:02:11.477 --> 00:02:13.119
four millilitres, below the mean.

00:02:13.764 --> 00:02:14.354
Check it forwards.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:17.222
Four ninety minus five oh eight point six

00:02:17.282 --> 00:02:19.904
four, over eight, is minus two point three

00:02:19.964 --> 00:02:22.725
three, and the tail is one minus zero

00:02:22.786 --> 00:02:24.246
point nine nine zero one,

00:02:24.987 --> 00:02:26.928
zero point zero zero nine nine.

00:02:27.573 --> 00:02:28.846
That's just under one percent.

00:02:29.531 --> 00:02:31.683
Fill two hundred bottles at this setting, and

00:02:31.723 --> 00:02:32.930
only two come up short.

00:02:33.613 --> 00:02:36.097
And the picture agrees: a higher mean moves

00:02:36.138 --> 00:02:38.562
the bell away from four ninety, so the

00:02:38.583 --> 00:02:39.163
tail shrinks.

00:02:40.107 --> 00:02:42.637
So, using the table's zed, a setting of

00:02:42.759 --> 00:02:44.687
five hundred and eight point six four is

00:02:44.748 --> 00:02:45.028
safe.

00:02:45.693 --> 00:02:46.918
If you round, round up.

00:02:47.508 --> 00:02:49.796
The spread can be the unknown instead.

00:02:50.519 --> 00:02:52.181
Bolts are made with a mean length of

00:02:52.282 --> 00:02:54.686
fifty millimetres, and a bolt is rejected if

00:02:54.727 --> 00:02:56.970
it's more than one millimetre from fifty.

00:02:57.673 --> 00:03:00.401
Right now sigma is zero point five, so

00:03:00.442 --> 00:03:02.106
the limits sit at two sigma,

00:03:02.609 --> 00:03:04.253
and about five percent are rejected.

00:03:04.997 --> 00:03:07.208
The maker wants that down to about zero

00:03:07.249 --> 00:03:07.972
point three percent.

00:03:08.677 --> 00:03:11.965
That means ninety-nine point seven percent inside, which

00:03:12.027 --> 00:03:12.848
is three sigma.

00:03:13.652 --> 00:03:16.142
So the one millimetre limits must be three

00:03:16.203 --> 00:03:17.929
standard deviations from the mean.

00:03:18.693 --> 00:03:21.419
Three sigma equals one, so sigma is one

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:22.522
third of a millimetre.

00:03:23.386 --> 00:03:26.499
Shrinking sigma squeezes the bell, and the tails

00:03:26.621 --> 00:03:27.604
pull inside the limits.

00:03:28.121 --> 00:03:30.293
When the percentage isn't on a whole sigma,

00:03:30.856 --> 00:03:31.399
use the table.

00:03:32.123 --> 00:03:34.979
Cereal boxes must hold at least three seventy-five

00:03:35.019 --> 00:03:35.341
grams.

00:03:35.803 --> 00:03:37.913
The mean is three eighty, and fewer than

00:03:37.953 --> 00:03:39.922
zero point five percent can be underweight.

00:03:40.747 --> 00:03:42.461
What's the largest sigma allowed?

00:03:43.647 --> 00:03:45.631
A left tail of zero point zero zero

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:48.577
five mirrors to zero point nine nine five

00:03:48.617 --> 00:03:49.038
to the left.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:51.963
The table gives zero point nine nine four

00:03:52.045 --> 00:03:53.847
nine at two point five seven,

00:03:54.389 --> 00:03:56.392
and zero point nine nine five one at

00:03:56.814 --> 00:03:59.659
two point five eight, so zed is about

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:01.743
minus two point five seven five.

00:04:02.645 --> 00:04:04.868
Then five over sigma is two point five

00:04:04.909 --> 00:04:07.834
seven five, so sigma is about one point

00:04:07.895 --> 00:04:08.796
nine four grams.

00:04:09.619 --> 00:04:12.004
To one decimal place, round down to one

00:04:12.045 --> 00:04:12.566
point nine.

00:04:13.349 --> 00:04:14.872
Round up to two, and the tail grows

00:04:14.893 --> 00:04:17.018
to about zero point six percent, which fails.

00:04:17.721 --> 00:04:19.567
So there are two levers for the same

00:04:19.628 --> 00:04:20.008
condition.

00:04:20.812 --> 00:04:23.279
Keep sigma at two grams instead, and the

00:04:23.341 --> 00:04:24.283
mean has to move up.

00:04:24.984 --> 00:04:29.146
Three seventy-five minus mu, over two, is minus

00:04:29.247 --> 00:04:30.748
two point five seven five,

00:04:31.389 --> 00:04:34.850
so mu is three seventy-five plus five point

00:04:34.932 --> 00:04:37.432
one five, which is three hundred and eighty

00:04:37.513 --> 00:04:38.333
point one five.

00:04:39.035 --> 00:04:41.441
That's just short, so round up to three

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:43.405
hundred and eighty point one six grams.

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:46.174
Either move the mean away from the limit,

00:04:46.616 --> 00:04:47.518
or shrink the spread.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:49.523
Here's a way to remember the method.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:53.434
Area to zed, then zed to the unknown.

00:04:54.157 --> 00:04:56.720
Find the zed from the probability first, then

00:04:56.861 --> 00:04:59.324
solve for the mean or sigma, and check

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:00.505
the direction on a sketch.

00:05:03.241 --> 00:05:03.730
Your turn.

00:05:04.219 --> 00:05:04.982
Find the mean.

00:05:05.586 --> 00:05:06.591
Pause here to answer.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.662
Two percent on the left mirrors to zero

00:05:19.702 --> 00:05:22.124
point nine eight, and zero point nine seven

00:05:22.164 --> 00:05:25.506
nine eight is closer, so zed is minus

00:05:25.566 --> 00:05:26.687
two point oh five,

00:05:27.508 --> 00:05:30.030
negative because a thousand grams is below the

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:30.350
mean.

00:05:31.111 --> 00:05:34.117
Sigma is three, so mu is a thousand

00:05:34.217 --> 00:05:37.142
plus six point one five, about one thousand

00:05:37.182 --> 00:05:38.645
and six point one five grams.

00:05:39.487 --> 00:05:41.795
A thousand minus six point one five is

00:05:42.117 --> 00:05:42.397
wrong.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:44.236
It puts the mean below the cut-off.

00:05:45.985 --> 00:05:46.410
Last one.

00:05:46.855 --> 00:05:47.825
Find sigma.

00:05:48.371 --> 00:05:49.257
Pause here to answer.

00:05:59.968 --> 00:06:03.293
Four percent above fifty-seven leaves zero point nine

00:06:03.394 --> 00:06:05.898
six below it, so zed is one point

00:06:05.939 --> 00:06:06.539
seven five,

00:06:07.121 --> 00:06:09.224
positive because fifty-seven is above the mean.

00:06:10.046 --> 00:06:12.407
Seven over sigma is one point seven five,

00:06:12.768 --> 00:06:14.409
so sigma is about four hours.

00:06:15.312 --> 00:06:17.520
A zed of minus one point seven five

00:06:17.641 --> 00:06:17.981
is wrong.

00:06:18.405 --> 00:06:20.959
It makes sigma negative, and a standard deviation

00:06:21.181 --> 00:06:21.784
can't be negative.

00:06:23.501 --> 00:06:25.707
So a probability fixes a zed score,

00:06:26.208 --> 00:06:28.534
and the zed score fixes the unknown mean

00:06:28.694 --> 00:06:29.136
or spread.

00:06:30.099 --> 00:06:32.228
That's the last of the normal distribution videos.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:34.777
You can now go from values to probabilities,

00:06:35.118 --> 00:06:37.043
and from probabilities back to the mean or

00:06:37.124 --> 00:06:37.445
sigma.

00:06:38.127 --> 00:06:40.356
Later practice videos mix these skills with the

00:06:40.416 --> 00:06:41.019
rest of the course.

00:06:43.688 --> 00:06:44.571
Here are the key notes.

00:06:45.094 --> 00:06:46.862
Pause the video if you need more time

00:06:46.883 --> 00:06:47.364
to copy them.
